{"headword":"בְּלִיַּ֫עַל","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>worthlessness (</strong>cpd. <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּלִי</span> <em>not, without</em> and <span dir=\"rtl\">יַעַל</span> <em>worth, use, profit</em><strong>)</strong>—<span dir=\"rtl\">בּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 13:14\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.13.14\">Dt 13:14</a> + 20 times; <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּלִיָּ֑עַל</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 101:3\" href=\"/Psalms.101.3\">ψ 101:3</a> + 5 times;—the quality of <em>being useless, good for nothing</em>."},{"senses":[{"definition":"abstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">אִישׁ (ה)בליעל</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">אַנְשֵׁי הבליעל</span>, <em>worthless, good-for-nothing, base fellows</em> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 25:25\" href=\"/I_Samuel.25.25\">1 S 25:25</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 16:7\" href=\"/II_Samuel.16.7\">2 S 16:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 20:1\" href=\"/II_Samuel.20.1\">20:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 21:13\" href=\"/I_Kings.21.13\">1 K 21:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 16:27\" href=\"/Proverbs.16.27\">Pr 16:27</a>; = <span dir=\"rtl\">בֶּן־ב׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 25:17\" href=\"/I_Samuel.25.17\">1 S 25:17</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּנֵי ב׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 13:14\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.13.14\">Dt 13:14</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 19:22\" href=\"/Judges.19.22\">Ju 19:22</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 20:13\" href=\"/Judges.20.13\">20:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 2:12\" href=\"/I_Samuel.2.12\">1 S 2:12</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 10:27\" href=\"/I_Samuel.10.27\">10:27</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 21:10\" href=\"/I_Kings.21.10\">1 K 21:10</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 21:13\" href=\"/I_Kings.21.13\">13</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 13:7\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.13.7\">2 Ch 13:7</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּת ב׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 1:16\" href=\"/I_Samuel.1.16\">1 S 1:16</a> (drunken woman); <span dir=\"rtl\">עֵד ב׳</span> <em>base witness</em> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 19:28\" href=\"/Proverbs.19.28\">Pr 19:28</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">דְּבַר ב׳</span> <em>base, wicked thing</em> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 41:9\" href=\"/Psalms.41.9\">ψ 41:9</a> (yet cf. <strong>3</strong> infr.), <a data-ref=\"Psalms 101:3\" href=\"/Psalms.101.3\">101:3</a> (add prob. also <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 29:10\" href=\"/I_Samuel.29.10\">1 S 29:10</a>, so 𝔊 We Dr); <span dir=\"rtl\">דָּבָר</span> … <span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳</span> (elliptical and in apposition) <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 15:9\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.15.9\">Dt 15:9</a>."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"concr. elliptical of <span dir=\"rtl\">אישׁ ב׳</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 23:6\" href=\"/II_Samuel.23.6\">2 S 23:6</a> <a data-ref=\"Job 34:18\" href=\"/Job.34.18\">Jb 34:18</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">כָּל־אִישׁ רַע וּבְלִיַּעַל</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 30:22\" href=\"/I_Samuel.30.22\">1 S 30:22</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אָדָם בְּלִיַּעַל</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 6:12\" href=\"/Proverbs.6.12\">Pr 6:12</a>."}],"num":"2."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>ruin, destruction:</em> so <a data-ref=\"Psalms 41:9\" href=\"/Psalms.41.9\">ψ 41:9</a> according to De Che al., but v. supr.; <span dir=\"rtl\">יֹעֵץ ב׳</span> <em>counsellor of ruin</em> <a data-ref=\"Nahum 1:11\" href=\"/Nahum.1.11\">Na 1:11</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳</span> alone <em>a man of ruin, destroyer</em> <a data-ref=\"Nahum 2:1\" href=\"/Nahum.2.1\">Na 2:1</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">נַחֲלֵי ב׳</span> <em>floods of destruction</em> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">שְׁאוֹל</span>) <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 22:5\" href=\"/II_Samuel.22.5\">2 S 22:5</a> = <a data-ref=\"Psalms 18:5\" href=\"/Psalms.18.5\">ψ 18:5</a>."}],"num":"3."}]},"rid":"BDB01254","strong_numbers":["1100"],"next_hw":"בִּלְעֲדֵי","prev_hw":"בְּלִימָה","all_cited":true,"occurrences":"27","quotes":[],"GK":["1175"],"TWOT":["246g"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}